// `+ Beat` in a when block brings the rules of the first when block of that
// beat. The beat runs up to that block (its content before it plays), and if
// one of its rules wins, the rest of that beat plays after the rule, then the
// rest of this one. The `if` of an insertion only decides whether it comes in.

state
  angry: true
  rich: false

beat Start
  Talk()
  angry = false
  Talk()
  rich = true
  Talk()
  angry = true
  Talk()
  After talks.

beat Talk
  when
    + Moods
    + Money if rich
    rich and angry
      Rich and angry.
    always
      Hello.
  Talk done.

beat Moods
  Moods prologue.

  when
    angry
      Get out!
    not angry
      Nice day.
  Moods epilogue.

beat Money
  when
    rich
      Nice purse.

/*
<test>
- expected: |
    ~ Moods prologue.

    ~ Get out!

    ~ Moods epilogue.

    ~ Talk done.

    ~ Moods prologue.

    ~ Nice day.

    ~ Moods epilogue.

    ~ Talk done.

    ~ Moods prologue.

    ~ Nice purse.

    ~ Talk done.

    ~ Moods prologue.

    ~ Rich and angry.

    ~ Talk done.

    ~ After talks.
</test>
*/
